{{!
    @template local_shopping_cart/history_body

    The list of previous purchases, without any card or panel around it.

    The checkout page renders it on the server when the data is already there, and shistory.js
    renders it into the history tab when the page loaded the history on demand.

    Classes required for JS:
    * cashier-history-items

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * historyitems Array of purchases
    * costcentercredits Array of credits per cost centre

    Example context (json):
    {
        "historyitems": [],
        "costcentercredits": []
    }
}}
<div class="history">
    {{! Before the <ul>, not inside it: a <button> is not a valid child of a
        list, and the credits manager is a control rather than a history
        entry. It used to be the first entry of the list, so it stays above
        it. The condition matches what costcentercredit_item used to
        check. }}
    {{^costcentercredits.0}}
        {{> local_shopping_cart/creditsmanager_button }}
    {{/costcentercredits.0}}
    <ul class="list-group cashier-history-items">
        {{> local_shopping_cart/costcentercredit_item }}
        {{> local_shopping_cart/history_items }}
    </ul>
</div>
